<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21991" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">impŏsĭtīcĭus</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inp-</span></b> ), or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		impono, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>laid on</i>, <i>applied</i> (anteand
			post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canthari,</span>”
				<i>only laid on</i>, <i>not fastened</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 30, 1, 41, § 11</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomina,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the primitive names applied to things</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 8, § 5</span></i>
			 Müll.; 10, § 61: causa, <i>ascribed</i> (opp. naturalis and publica), <i><span class="en">Dig. 39, 1, 5, § 9</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
